<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  COLLECTION empty-state illustration.

  Frozen canonical: `COLLECTION pusto` > `Collection List` > `Track Item 1`,
  where `Circle` is a 166x166 box at (96,55) and `Frame 5` a 46x46 badge at
  (211,157). The badge sits entirely inside the disc's bounding box, so the whole
  illustration is one 166x166 drawable and the badge is placed at (115,102)
  within it.

  Every box below is verbatim from the export:

    disc / outer ring   139.79 at (13.11,13.11)   -> r 69.895 at (83.005,83.005)
    disc / inner ring   111    at (27,27.5)       -> r 55.5   at (82.5,83)
    disc / hub           54    at (56,56)         -> r 27     at (83,83)
    disc / spindle       14    at (76,76)         -> r 7      at (83,83)
    badge / plate        46    at (115,102)       -> r 23     at (138,125)
    badge / heart     23.8x21.69 at (126.1,115.22)

  Two things are authored rather than measured, and both are forced.

  **The shapes are circles.** The exporter records a vector's box and its fills
  but never its geometry, so no path data for any of these six exists in the
  repository. Four of them are the rings of a record and are unambiguous. The
  46x46 badge plate is not: its silhouette carries no path data either, and the
  one preview that renders this frame - tools/figma-export/dark-theme/previews/
  dark-collection-empty.png, an earlier revision - does not draw it at all. A
  circle is what the rest of the illustration is made of and what a square
  bounding box with no other evidence gives, so a circle is what it is.

  **The heart is Material's `favorite`.** The frozen node carries no path either,
  but Frame 5 also holds a hidden second heart at exactly 20x18.35 - which is the
  bounding box of Material's `favorite` path to the decimal. So the family is not
  a guess. That path is placed here through a group transform that maps its
  source box (2,3)-(22,21.35) onto the visible heart's 23.8x21.69 at (126.1,
  115.22): scale 1.19 / 1.182016, translate 123.72 / 111.674. Both corners land
  exactly.

  Colours are illustration-specific and stay out of the semantic token system -
  see the block in values/colors.xml. The two rings are the only ones the design
  changes between the themes; the rest have no night variant on purpose.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="166dp"
    android:height="166dp"
    android:viewportWidth="166"
    android:viewportHeight="166">

    <path
        android:fillColor="@color/collection_empty_disc_outer"
        android:pathData="M13.11,83.005 a69.895,69.895 0 1,0 139.79,0 a69.895,69.895 0 1,0 -139.79,0 Z" />
    <path
        android:fillColor="@color/collection_empty_disc_inner"
        android:pathData="M27,83 a55.5,55.5 0 1,0 111,0 a55.5,55.5 0 1,0 -111,0 Z" />
    <path
        android:fillColor="@color/collection_empty_disc_hub"
        android:pathData="M56,83 a27,27 0 1,0 54,0 a27,27 0 1,0 -54,0 Z" />
    <path
        android:fillColor="@color/collection_empty_disc_spindle"
        android:pathData="M76,83 a7,7 0 1,0 14,0 a7,7 0 1,0 -14,0 Z" />

    <path
        android:fillColor="@color/collection_empty_badge_plate"
        android:pathData="M115,125 a23,23 0 1,0 46,0 a23,23 0 1,0 -46,0 Z" />

    <group
        android:scaleX="1.19"
        android:scaleY="1.182016"
        android:translateX="123.72"
        android:translateY="111.674">
        <path
            android:fillColor="@color/collection_empty_badge_heart"
            android:pathData="M12,21.35l-1.45,-1.32C5.4,15.36 2,12.28 2,8.5 2,5.42 4.42,3 7.5,3c1.74,0 3.41,0.81 4.5,2.09C13.09,3.81 14.76,3 16.5,3 19.58,3 22,5.42 22,8.5c0,3.78 -3.4,6.86 -8.55,11.54L12,21.35z" />
    </group>
</vector>
